00:20:25.191 --> 00:20:48.749
And this was really a point that was very, very important to Jung and a staple of his therapeutic approach, for which I have a quote here. Loneliness does not come from having no people about one, but from being unable to communicate the things that seem important to oneself. So what he would, for example, do is take people seriously.

00:20:49.543 --> 00:21:04.758
Which means when people come with psychological conditions and visions, convictions, all these different things, that he would listen and say like, it's already often enough that one other human being is listening and taking it seriously what another human being is saying.

