00:27:20.914 --> 00:27:37.230
The dream falls in my own shadow where my light fails. It is just as though I had never heard of dream analysis. That is, of course, the maddening thing, that you are never equal to your own dreams. I have to begin at the very beginning and come to the most painstaking analysis.

00:27:38.744 --> 00:28:02.715
So when we talk to other people, there's a lot of things that we do not really anticipate, and it's valuable because they can give us a different perspective on things based on their own experience or just by paying attention. And asking like, oh, why didn't you do this? Have you thought maybe about this? And this is then actually pretty precisely dealing with those blind spots.

00:28:03.565 --> 00:28:19.435
And I see it that the cards can be used in a similar way, that when you lay the cards for yourself, that it can go like, oh, have you thought about this situation in this way? Have you thought about maybe about this? So it is a kind of discussion that you can do with yourself.

00:28:20.513 --> 00:28:38.183
Through the cards, which is super interesting because again, it's about exploring, mapping the psyche, paying attention, integrating things that one is not aware of. So similar as one runs a conversation with a person, it's possible to, to run a conversation with the cards, with yourself.

