00:29:18.190 --> 00:29:37.768
It has to do with the fact that maybe I don't know everything, and very likely the things I don't know don't make sense, but they only don't make sense to me. Jung says what our consciousness can do extremely well is it can exclude very, very well.

00:29:38.321 --> 00:30:01.923
So inside our consciousness, so the things we know, what we can do and so on, everything seems very logical, very coherent, and it's a kind of ideology, ideology in the sense of there exists nothing outside. So everything outside is not important. Like only these things are important, but at the same time, our consciousness is incomplete.

00:30:02.136 --> 00:30:19.716
We hit our head constantly and we should be aware of the fact like, okay, it's not working. What we know and what we can do is, it's not enough. So being open for, let's say, messages of the universe that are kind of pointing things out to you, like pay attention to that, is in a sense a good approach.

00:30:20.438 --> 00:30:37.666
